      "summaries": {
        "en": "This project provides the code for the book 'Machine Learning for Algorithmic Trading', offering a comprehensive guide to applying ML in finance. It covers data preparation, feature engineering, model selection, and backtesting using real-world market data. Key strengths include practical Jupyter Notebooks with step-by-step implementations of strategies like regression, classification, and reinforcement learning. Use it to learn end-to-end ML workflows for trading, experiment with synthetic data, or build your own trading agents.",
        "zh": "该项目是《Machine Learning for Algorithmic Trading》第二版的配套代码库，提供从数据获取、特征工程、模型训练到回测评估的完整端到端工作流。核心亮点在于使用Jupyter Notebook展示实操代码，涵盖回归、分类、强化学习等多种策略，并包含合成数据生成工具。通过它可快速掌握金融领域ML应用，学习构建交易信号、管理风险及训练交易智能体，为初学者和从业者提供从理论到实践的清晰路径。",
        "es": "This project provides the code for the book 'Machine Learning for Algorithmic Trading', offering a comprehensive guide to applying ML in finance. It covers data preparation, feature engineering, model selection, and backtesting using real-world market data. Key strengths include practical Jupyter Notebooks with step-by-step implementations of strategies like regression, classification, and reinforcement learning. Use it to learn end-to-end ML workflows for trading, experiment with synthetic data, or build your own trading agents.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "machine-learning-for-trading stands out for artificial-intelligence, data-science, and deep-learning in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "This project provides the code for the book 'Machine Learning for Algorithmic Trading', offering a comprehensive guide to applying ML in finance. It covers data preparation, feature engineering, model selection, and backtesting using real-world market data. Key strengths include practical Jupyter Notebooks with step-by-step implementations of strategies like regression, classification, and reinforcement learning. Use it to learn end-to-end ML workflows for trading, experiment with synthetic data, or build your own trading agents.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/stefan-jansen/machine-learning-for-trading for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
